// VMFL051-R3 -- THE FROZEN SAMPLING RULE (PREREGISTRATION.md sections 3.2, 3.4).
//
// CHANGED from R2 (PREREGISTRATION.md section 2): R2's two cellZones (gateZone,
// gateZoneInner) are KEPT UNCHANGED so their volume-average diagnostics remain
// available, and TWO cross-plane faceZones are ADDED -- `postExpPlane` (the R3
// GATE) and `postExpPlane2` (a plane-sensitivity DIAGNOSTIC that gates nothing).
//
// The R3 gate is the mass-flux-weighted (conservative) reduction on a downstream
// cross-plane inside the uniform post-expansion wedge, clear of the fan.  Every
// coordinate below is derived from case INPUTS -- M1 = 2.5, the 15 deg turn,
// gamma = 1.3990093734749485, the domain bounds, and a conservative Mach bound
// M_cons = 3.5 chosen larger than any physically plausible answer -- and from NO
// solved output, which is what makes the planes ANSWER-BLIND.
//
// Cross-plane construction (PREREGISTRATION.md section 3.2), for each station:
//   station x_p is a cell FACE at every level (0.6 and 0.9 land exactly on the
//   downstream-block face grid: 0.6/dx and 0.9/dx are integers for nxB in
//   {96,192,384}), so a THIN x-slab [x_p - delta, x_p + delta] with
//   delta = 5.0e-4 m < half the finest cell width (L3 half-dx = 1.5625e-3 m)
//   captures EXACTLY ONE COLUMN of x-normal internal faces whose centres sit at
//   x = x_p.  The y-band is the middle 50 % of the CONSERVATIVE wedge:
//     wall           y_wall  = -x_p*tan(15 deg)
//     trailing ray   y_tr    = +x_p*tan(asin(1/M_cons) - 15 deg),  M_cons = 3.5
//     H_cons = y_tr - y_wall;  band = [y_wall + 0.25*H, y_wall + 0.75*H]
//   The true trailing ray (at the analytic M2 ~ 3.2355) sits ABOVE the
//   conservative one for every M2 < 3.5, so the band lies inside the true uniform
//   wedge for every physically possible answer.  z bounds (-1,+1) enclose the
//   +/-0.01 m slab with room to spare.
//
// postExpPlane  (GATE)        x_p  = 0.60 m  y in [-0.116385, -0.027615]
// postExpPlane2 (DIAGNOSTIC)  x_p2 = 0.90 m  y in [-0.174577, -0.041422]
//
// A faceZone is built as a faceSet (boxToFace, faces by centre) converted to a
// faceZone (setToFaceZone) -- the v2606 idiom.  surfaceFieldValue reads the
// faceZone with regionType faceZone; scalar weightedAverage is orientation-
// independent (the weight is mag(phi)), so the faceZone flip map does not affect
// the graded value.

actions
(
    // ---- R2 cellZones, KEPT UNCHANGED (volume diagnostics only) -------------
    {
        name    gateZone;
        type    cellZoneSet;
        action  new;
        source  boxToCell;
        box     (1.00 -0.1929491924311227 -1) (1.15 -0.02253916841837858 1);
    }
    {
        name    gateZoneInner;
        type    cellZoneSet;
        action  new;
        source  boxToCell;
        box     (1.00 -0.1579491924311227 -1) (1.15 -0.05753916841837858 1);
    }

    // ---- R3 GATE cross-plane at x_p = 0.60 m --------------------------------
    {
        name    postExpPlaneFaces;
        type    faceSet;
        action  new;
        source  boxToFace;
        box     (0.5995 -0.116385 -1) (0.6005 -0.027615 1);
    }
    {
        name    postExpPlane;
        type    faceZoneSet;
        action  new;
        source  setToFaceZone;
        faceSet postExpPlaneFaces;
    }

    // ---- R3 DIAGNOSTIC cross-plane at x_p2 = 0.90 m (gates nothing) ---------
    {
        name    postExpPlane2Faces;
        type    faceSet;
        action  new;
        source  boxToFace;
        box     (0.8995 -0.174577 -1) (0.9005 -0.041422 1);
    }
    {
        name    postExpPlane2;
        type    faceZoneSet;
        action  new;
        source  setToFaceZone;
        faceSet postExpPlane2Faces;
    }
);
